    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d547">

                <pb facs="0476" n="360" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg360"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/1028.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Blanchard to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 18, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Had an interview this evening by appointment with President Theodore at which
                    Minister of Foreign Affairs and Chief of Protocol and later Minister of the
                    Interior were present. Complied with your instructions of November 12, 2 p.m.
                    and November 16, 11 a.m. The President seems quite disposed to appointment of
                    commission but insists in such case on recognition, not as Provisional President
                    but as President, having been, as stated in my November 13, 3 p.m., regularly
                    elected by the National Assembly in accordance with Haitian Constitution. His
                    views emphatically sustained by members of Cabinet present. Under these
                    circumstances strongly recommend granting recognition as President upon
                    appointment of commission as outlined. Respectfully submit advisability early
                    favorable opinion to avail of their present seemingly good disposition.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Blanchard</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
